# Build output
/bin/
/out/
*.test
coverage.out

# The demo boards are test fixtures, so only what the tests read is kept: the
# board itself, the project file (net classes), the custom rules, and the
# schematics the parser is exercised against. Everything KiCad generates or
# vendors is left out -- for each board that is 203 MB against 5 MB of actual
# design. demo-pcb-2 is the same board further through routing, and is kept
# under the same rules.

# 101 MB of vendored LCSC symbols, footprints and 3D models
demo-pcb*/libs/
# 100 MB of pcbnew autosave archives
demo-pcb*/ai-vision-backups/
# generated gerbers, drill files and netlist
demo-pcb*/out/
# pcbnew's in-progress copy of the board
demo-pcb*/_autosave-*
# editor lock files, present only while KiCad has the project open
demo-pcb*/~*.lck
# per-user editor state: which layers are visible, where the view was
demo-pcb*/*.kicad_prl

# The KiCad plugin's generated half: the engine binary and the built report
kicad-plugin/bin/
kicad-plugin/web/
kicad-plugin/**/__pycache__/
kicad-plugin/.pytest_cache/
/dist/

# Webapp build output and installed packages
webapp/node_modules/
webapp/dist/

.DS_Store
